omaddons --help lists every command with what it does
==> omaddons --help <==
omaddons 0.1.0 · World of Warcraft addon manager for Linux

Usage: omaddons [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Look (changes no addon):
  status                         Triage every client: addons, updates, issues, backups
  list, ls                       List the addons in each target's AddOns folder
  outdated, check                Show which managed addons have updates
  info, show                     Show what an addon is and where it is installed
  search, find                   Find addons in the catalog, WoWInterface, Tukui and GitHub
  errors                         Show which addons throw Lua errors, from BugGrabber
  export                         Print every client's addon set as one addons.toml
  history, log                   Show what changed, when, by whom and why
  plans                          Inspect a stored plan and whether it was applied
  net-log                        List the network requests and git runs omaddons made
  doctor                         Find what is broken in what omaddons manages

Change (preview any with --dry-run):
  install, add                   Install or update addons on one client
  update, upgrade                Update managed addons on every client
  pin                            Hold an addon at its release through updates
  unpin                          Let a pinned addon update again
  adopt                          Bring addons installed by hand under management
  sync                           Make every client match addons.toml
  copy                           Install one client's addons on another
  remove, uninstall, rm, delete  Remove managed addons from one client
  undo, revert, rollback         Revert the last change, or one by its id
  apply                          Run exactly the plan a --dry-run stored
  backup                         Back up, list and restore each client's WTF/ settings

Setup:
  targets                        List the WoW clients, or add, remove, rename and choose them
  config                         Show or change config.toml
  auth                           Store, check or clear the opt-in GitHub token
  omarchy                        Put the omaddons widget on Omarchy's bar
  completions                    Print a shell completion script
  install-completions            Install the completion script where your shell looks for it
  robot-docs                     Print documentation for agents
  capabilities                   Describe everything this build can do, for agents
  help                           Show help for omaddons or one command

Global options:
      --json              One JSON envelope on stdout
      --robot             The same as --json
      --format <FORMAT>   Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>   The client to act on: id, game mode, family, path, or all [alias:
                          --flavor]
      --dry-run           Show the plan without changing anything
      --actor <ACTOR>     Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>     Why, recorded verbatim in history
      --offline           Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running     Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --if-match <TOKEN>  Run only what the preview that returned this token showed
      --no-color          No ANSI color
      --no-progress       No progress output
      --progress <MODE>   Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet             Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...        More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help              Show help
  -V, --version           Show the version

Environment:
  OMADDONS_ACTOR         Default --actor: human, agent or widget
  OMADDONS_OFFLINE       1 (exactly) means --offline
  OMADDONS_FORMAT        json means --json
  OMADDONS_GITHUB_TOKEN  Bearer token sent to api.github.com only
  NO_COLOR               Set and non-empty: no color
  CI                     Set and non-empty: no color, and NDJSON on stderr
  TERM                   dumb: no color, and NDJSON on stderr
  HOME                   Required and absolute: every path omaddons derives starts here
  XDG_CONFIG_HOME        Moves omaddons' config when absolute; also the Lutris and Heroic config
                         lookups
  XDG_STATE_HOME         Moves omaddons' state when absolute
  XDG_CACHE_HOME         Moves omaddons' cache when absolute
  XDG_DATA_HOME          Moves the Lutris, Steam and Bottles data lookups; omaddons keeps no files
                         there
  OMARCHY_PATH           Where omarchy install also looks for Omarchy's shell ($OMARCHY_PATH/shell)
  PATH                   Where gh, git and omarchy-shell are found; git keeps only PATH from the
                         caller's environment
  Debug builds also read OMADDONS_FAILPOINTS, OMADDONS_FAILPOINT_DIR, OMADDONS_HTTP_FIXTURES,
  OMADDONS_RECORD, OMADDONS_PROC_ROOT, OMADDONS_NOW, OMADDONS_FS_CLONE, OMADDONS_FS_FREE_MB,
  OMADDONS_WIDGET_ID, OMADDONS_TEST_FIXERS

